0040-import-and-download-never-delete-first.patch -- a game dump is replaced only by a complete new file (docs/REVIEW-TRIAGE-2026-11-19.md, finding 3.1).
Applied by scripts/build-app.sh to its copy of the C# snapshot (patch -p1, run in the project folder), after 0010, 0020 and whatever lies between (0030-0039 belong to other work); app/gameapp/ is not edited.
UNTESTED ON DEVICE: written without a C# compiler; File.Move(string, string, bool) is the overload GameAppMods.WriteState already uses.
  * GameAppMain.cs CopyIn (the only import path of .nsp/.xci/.nsz/.nup): the old code deleted the existing dump FIRST, then moved the new file in; a move that failed (anything but an
    IOException, or a copy that ran out of disk) lost both. Now the file lands as <name>.part and replaces the old one in one rename; a failure removes the .part and leaves the old dump.
  * GameAppLibrary.cs CopyWithProgress (download from iCloud / Files, upload to a folder) and GameAppNas.cs Download: the .part was complete before the old destination was deleted, so
    the window was small, but the delete is gone (one rename over the old file) and a failed copy no longer leaves a multi-GB .part behind.
